Fovea temporal (dev/0.7-fovea-temporal, native/quadviews/dcsvr_gaze.h, dcsvr_perception.h, dcsvr_live.h): two keys, both
live (settings.cfg), both off by default (the layer as before).
- dcsvr_gaze_glide_ms (0-200, default 0): outside saccades a move of the focus (the gaze leaving the deadzone, drift,
  pursuit) is shown as an exponential approach with this time constant instead of a step in one frame. At fixation the
  eye is not suppressed and a step moved the focus edge's blend band (0.5 degree of a ramp about 8 degrees wide: up to
  ~10 % of the focus/periphery difference at once) and the focus view's projection in the same frame: seen as a flash at
  the border. Saccades, gaps and moves over 2 degrees still jump. Gaze statistics line: "; glided N (glide G ms)".
- dcsvr_temporal_saccade_reset (default 1): 0 keeps the periphery stability's history through saccades. The reset was
  taken as free (vision suppressed), but it is decided at the gaze's display time and with frame generation that frame
  is seen 55-90 ms later, after the landing: the ring just outside the new focus edge showed unfiltered for a frame and
  settled over the next two or three, on every saccade (54-89 per 30 s in the 2026-11-23 flight). Periphery stability
  lines: "kept through saccades" on the "on" line, "; saccade frames kept N" on the 30 s line.
